-### SWAGS
-A method that divides the dynamic sequence into different windows based on motion amount, training separate dynamic 3DGS models in different windows with different canonical spaces and deformation fields [S1]. The deformation field uses a tunable MLP that focuses more on modeling the dynamic part of the scene [S1]. Fine-tuning ensures temporal consistency between windows using overlapping frames to add constraints. The MLP is fixed and only the canonical representation is optimized during fine-tuning [S1].
